            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerns a Ninth Circuit rule on guilty pleas that the United States argues is a new constitutional rule not required by the Constitution and that would complicate and expose guilty pleas to collateral attack."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8e1374e565aaa336cc40007e979efb655dcd3ced68197499cff25368bb83846e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8e1374e565aa-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, the United States also notes that the rule would stifle the market for plea bargains, which the Court has described as an essential component of the administration of justice."
      }
    ],
